  "summary": "Four candidate documents directly apply multilevel probabilistic models with partial pooling (Bayesian hierarchical models) to predicting protein molecular function, making them the most relevant to the research question. [V0164] (Fischer et al., 2022) applies the method to the MetroFlow dataset, reporting a test F1 of 0.87. [V0163] (El-Sayed et al., 2021) applies the method to the ChurnBench dataset, reporting an AUROC of 0.80. [V0162] (Duarte et al., 2020) applies the method to the FireScope dataset, reporting an MAE of 0.73. [V0161] (Chen et al., 2019) applies the method to the ProtMap dataset, reporting an accuracy of 0.66. A fifth slot is filled by [V0068] (Brennan et al., 2018), which applies multilevel probabilistic models with partial pooling but to fraud detection rather than protein function, making it the next closest methodological match despite the topic mismatch. Documents that only mention the method as prior work (e.g., [V0064], [V0055], [V0034], [V0221]) are excluded as they do not constitute direct applications.",
